BOPAlgo_PaveFiller::PerformFF: each face/face pair is intersected in an
IntTools_Context of its own, which built the surface adaptors of both faces
(IntTools_Context::SurfaceAdaptor, restricted to the UV bounds of the face,
BRepTools::UVBounds, which goes through all edges of the face) for every
pair: a face with thousands of edges paired with many faces took seconds to
minutes. The adaptor of each face is built once and the context of each
pair gets a shallow copy of it (the new IntTools_Context::SetSurfaceAdaptor);
the copies are what the contexts built before, so the result is unchanged.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/BOPAlgo/BOPAlgo_PaveFiller_6.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/BOPAlgo/BOPAlgo_PaveFiller_6.cxx
